  "unit": "People per 100 members of the selected population aged 15–24.",
  "population": "People ages 15–24. Women and men use the population and labor force of the same age and sex. The total uses the published rates for all people ages 15–24.",
  "definitions": "The labor force consists of employed and unemployed persons. Unemployment generally requires being without employment, seeking work and available for work. People outside the labor force are in neither category.",
  "formula": {
    "p": "Published participation rate, percent of this population aged 15–24.",
    "u": "Published youth unemployment rate, percent of this group’s labor force ages 15–24.",
    "impliedEmployed": "p × (1 − u / 100)",
    "unemployed": "p × u / 100",
    "outsideLaborForce": "100 − p"
  },
  "reportedEmployment": "The published youth employment-to-population ratio is the percentage of the selected population ages 15–24 in employment. The download retains that estimate alongside the employed share calculated from the published participation and unemployment rates. Source rounding can produce small differences.",
  "missingValues": "Blank means unavailable. Participation alone yields the outside share. Employed and unemployed shares require both participation and unemployment. All three complete calculated shares sum to 100 before display rounding.",
  "interpretation": "Annual estimates describe employment status. The source does not identify whether someone outside the labor force attends school or training. People ages 15–24 also belong to the comparison population aged 15 and older. The ILO combines nationally reported data with modeled estimates. The WDI extract provides no country-year imputation flag. The publisher cautions against country comparisons and rankings based on imputed figures.",
  "references": [
    "https://databank.worldbank.org/metadataglossary/world-development-indicators/series/SL.TLF.ACTI.1524.ZS",
    "https://databank.worldbank.org/metadataglossary/world-development-indicators/series/SL.UEM.1524.ZS",
